Added `plone-client mcp --http`, which serves the MCP server over streamable HTTP for assistants that connect to a URL. Every request needs a bearer token, made with `plone-client mcp-token generate` and kept in the keyring, or given in `PLONE_CLIENT_MCP_TOKEN`. The server listens on `127.0.0.1:8000` unless given `--host` and `--port`, and the sites' own credentials stay in its profiles. @ericof
